WEBVTT

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:02.760
Found a great article for your students?

00:00:03.118 --> 00:00:06.198
The VU Education Lab AI Assistant turns it into teaching

00:00:06.198 --> 00:00:08.738
material, right beside the page.

00:00:12.949 --> 00:00:15.009
Setting up takes a minute.

00:00:15.009 --> 00:00:17.189
The welcome page walks you through it.

00:00:17.489 --> 00:00:19.309
Open the panel beside a page,

00:00:19.309 --> 00:00:21.909
then sign in with your VU Amsterdam email.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.620
There's no password, just a code in your inbox.

00:00:27.699 --> 00:00:28.899
And you're in.

00:00:29.179 --> 00:00:30.599
Sixteen tools, in four groups:

00:00:30.599 --> 00:00:33.039
understand the text, assess your students,

00:00:33.039 --> 00:00:35.159
design your teaching, or ask anything.

00:00:39.249 --> 00:00:40.569
Open any page.

00:00:41.081 --> 00:00:43.961
Here it's a VU Amsterdam news article about wildfires,

00:00:43.961 --> 00:00:47.161
and the panel picks it up straight away.

00:00:47.186 --> 00:00:49.326
Each tool has a few simple options,

00:00:49.326 --> 00:00:50.946
like length or audience.

00:00:51.278 --> 00:00:54.278
Let's make twelve slides, with speaker notes and a script

00:00:54.278 --> 00:00:55.758
for a knowledge clip.

00:00:56.531 --> 00:00:58.311
The slides stream in, in Dutch,

00:00:58.311 --> 00:01:01.031
because that's the language set for this course.

00:01:02.389 --> 00:01:04.969
One click exports the slides to PowerPoint.

00:01:05.384 --> 00:01:07.764
They use the official VU Amsterdam template,

00:01:07.764 --> 00:01:10.144
with the script in the speaker notes.

00:01:12.139 --> 00:01:14.019
Everything you make stays in your history,

00:01:14.019 --> 00:01:15.679
on your own device.

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:22.620
What makes the material fit is your course profile.

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:24.720
Import one straight from Canvas.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:27.800
The assistant reads the course material you can see,

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:29.240
never students, grades or submissions,

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:31.080
and drafts a profile.

00:01:31.634 --> 00:01:33.714
Description, learning objectives,

00:01:33.754 --> 00:01:35.834
Bloom levels, weekly structure and assessment:

00:01:35.834 --> 00:01:37.834
edit anything you like.

00:01:38.214 --> 00:01:41.674
From then on, every tool writes for your course.

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:45.290
In Settings, choose English or Dutch,

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:50.790
light or dark, and a faster or stronger AI model.

00:01:51.151 --> 00:01:53.851
The assistant only reads the page you have open.

00:01:54.171 --> 00:01:57.551
Page text is processed in the EU and never stored.

00:02:01.333 --> 00:02:03.053
You can also just ask.

00:02:03.307 --> 00:02:05.587
On Alan Turing's Wikipedia page,

00:02:05.587 --> 00:02:08.167
we ask how the article relates to our course.

00:02:08.756 --> 00:02:11.456
The answer names the course topics and learning objectives

00:02:11.456 --> 00:02:12.896
it supports.

00:02:13.385 --> 00:02:14.945
Keep going with a follow-up question,

00:02:14.945 --> 00:02:16.925
or ask for a change.

00:02:23.422 --> 00:02:26.662
The plus button adds a document or another open tab as a

00:02:26.662 --> 00:02:27.482
source.

00:02:28.622 --> 00:02:30.202
Now a quiz bank.

00:02:30.582 --> 00:02:33.662
Choose the question types, difficulty and audience.

00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:37.048
Each question comes with a rationale,

00:02:37.088 --> 00:02:39.488
a quote from the source, its Bloom level and an

00:02:39.488 --> 00:02:41.108
item-quality check.

00:02:41.508 --> 00:02:43.128
Keep what works, edit the rest,

00:02:43.128 --> 00:02:45.468
and export to Canvas, Moodle,

00:02:45.468 --> 00:02:48.448
Wooclap, Kahoot, Mentimeter or TestVision.

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:52.460
The VU Education Lab AI Assistant.

00:02:53.075 --> 00:02:55.615
For VU Amsterdam staff and students.

00:02:56.186 --> 00:03:01.326
Install it from teacher-assistant.vu-edulab.nl.
